<title>UK: Banque Indosuez, Paris wins Reuter Nov forex poll.</title>
<headline>Banque Indosuez, Paris wins Reuter Nov forex poll.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Indosuez in Paris has won the Reuter foreign exchange poll for November beating 40 other banks and financial institutions from around the globe.</p>
<p>The levels predicted by Banque Indosuez gave them an average divergence from the actual rates of 0.4472 percent.</p>
<p>In second place was Lehman Brothers in London with an average divergence of 0.6455 followed by Bank of Montreal, Toronto in third place with 0.8437 percent.</p>
<p>The average divergence rates of the 40 polled varied between 0.4472 and 3.8952 percent.</p>
<p>The rankings were based on the accuracy of the forecasts against the European closing rates on November 29 of dollar/mark at 1.5380, dollar/yen at 113.83 and sterling/dollar at 1.6813.</p>
<p>Only two forecasters polled expected dollar/sterling to rise above 1.6800, with the highest rate predicted at 1.6900.</p>
<p>Six percent of those polled expected dollar/mark to rise above 1.5300. The highest level predicted was 1.5500.</p>
<p>The highest dollar/yen level expected during November was 117.00, the lowest expected was 111.00.</p>
